{% extends 'user/Academics/program_detail.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Bachelor of Science in Civil Engineering{% endblock %}

{% block default_hero_image %}images/Academics/bsce.png{% endblock %}

{% block overview_default %}
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-lg mb-6">
    The Bachelor of Science in Civil Engineering (BSCE) is a four-year program that aims to provide students with knowledge in mathematics and science to be applied in the different specializations such as structural, transportation, water resource, geotechnical, environmental and construction project management.
</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-lg">
    Students are trained to develop exceptional skills in planning, design, supervision, and implementation of infrastructures and civil engineering works.
</p>
{% endblock %}

{% block objectives_default %}
<p class="text-slate-600 text-lg mb-8">
    Three to five years after graduation, the Civil Engineering alumni shall have:
</p>
<div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-[2rem] p-6 border border-slate-100">
        <h3 class="font-black text-feu-green mb-4 uppercase">Professional Growth</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-justify">Engaged in the practice of Civil Engineering, specifically on the different specializations on structural engineering, water resources engineering, construction engineering and management, geotechnical engineering and transportation engineering, or technopreneurship and innovation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-[2rem] p-6 border border-slate-100">
        <h3 class="font-black text-feu-green mb-4 uppercase">Leadership</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-justify">Assumed significant roles with key responsibilities in their workplace.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-[2rem] p-6 border border-slate-100">
        <h3 class="font-black text-feu-green mb-4 uppercase">Organizations</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-justify">Involved themselves in professional, socio-civic, government, or non-government activities.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-[2rem] p-6 border border-slate-100">
        <h3 class="font-black text-feu-green mb-4 uppercase">Community Impact</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-justify">Demonstrated continuous professional development through certifications, attendance to training, seminars, and conferences and/or pursuit of graduate studies in engineering or related fields.</p>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}

{% block outcomes_description_default %}
What every engineering graduate is expected to demonstrate
{% endblock %}

{% block outcomes_default %}
<div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    {% set outcomes = [
        'Apply knowledge of mathematics, natural science, engineering fundamentals and an engineering specialization to the solution of complex engineering problems.',
        'Conduct investigations of complex engineering problems using research-based knowledge and research methods including design of experiments, analysis and interpretation of data, and synthesis of information to provide valid conclusions.',
        'Design solutions for complex engineering problems and design systems, components or processes that meet specified needs with appropriate consideration for public health and safety, cultural, societal, and environmental considerations.',
        'Function effectively as an individual, and as a member or leader in diverse teams and in multi-disciplinary settings.',
        'Identify, formulate, research literature and analyze complex engineering problems reaching substantiated conclusions using first principles of mathematics, natural sciences and engineering sciences.',
        'Apply ethical principles and commit to professional ethics and responsibilities and norms of engineering practice.',
        'Communicate effectively on complex engineering activities with the engineering community and with society at large, such as being able to comprehend and write effective reports and design documentation, make effective presentations, and give and receive clear instructions.',
        'Understand and evaluate the sustainability and impact of professional engineering work in the solution of complex engineering problems in societal and environmental context.',
        'Recognize the need for, and have the preparation and ability to engage in independent and life-long learning in the broadest context of technological change.',
        'Apply reasoning informed by contextual knowledge to assess societal, health, safety, legal and cultural issues and the consequent responsibilities relevant to professional engineering practice and solutions to complex engineering problems.',
        'Create, select and apply appropriate techniques, resources, and modern engineering and IT tools, including prediction and modelling, to complex engineering problems with an understanding of the limitations.',
        'Demonstrate knowledge and understanding of engineering management principles and economic decision-making and apply these to one’s own work, as a member and leader in a team, to manage projects and in multidisciplinary environments.'
    ] %}
    {% for item in outcomes %}
        <div class="bg-white/10 rounded-2xl p-5 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/10">
            <div class="flex gap-4">
                <span class="bg-feu-yellow text-feu-green w-10 h-10 shrink-0 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-black text-sm">
                    {{ range('A', 'Z')[loop.index0]|default(loop.index) }}
                </span>
                <p class="text-white/90 leading-relaxed">{{ item }}</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    {% endfor %}
</div>
{% endblock %}

{% block attributes_default %}
<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
    {% set attributes = [
        'Engineering Knowledge',
        'Problem Analysis',
        'Design Development',
        'Investigation',
        'Modern Tool Usage',
        'Environment & Sustainability',
        'Ethics',
        'Communication',
        'Project Management',
        'Lifelong Learning'
    ] %}
    {% for item in attributes %}
        <div class="competency-pill px-6 py-4 rounded-full font-bold shadow-md">{{ item }}</div>
    {% endfor %}
</div>
{% endblock %}

{% block specializations_default %}
<div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-[2rem] p-6 border border-slate-100">
        <h3 class="font-black text-feu-green mb-4 uppercase">Structural Engineering</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600">A sub-discipline of BSCE that focuses on the design and analysis of structural system to resist loads, stresses, and pressures from environmental and external sources such as earthquake, and wind to ensure the safety of the occupants throughout its lifespan.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-[2rem] p-6 border border-slate-100">
        <h3 class="font-black text-feu-green mb-4 uppercase">Water Resources Engineering</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600">A sub-discipline of BSCE that focuses on the study of hydrologic cycle and movement of water in the atmosphere and land surface. In addition, the hydraulic engineering responses through infrastructure development, design, and construction includes water supply system, sewerage, flood control and drainage, irrigation, and hydropower.</p>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}

{% block careers_default %}
<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
    {% set careers = [
        'Construction Field',
        'Construction Project Management',
        'Environmental Engineering',
        'Geotechnical Engineering',
        'Oil and Gas',
        'Structural Design',
        'Water Resources'
    ] %}
    {% for item in careers %}
        <div class="careers-pill px-6 py-4 rounded-full font-bold shadow-md">{{ item }}</div>
    {% endfor %}
</div>
{% endblock %}

{% block laboratories_default %}
<div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center bg-white rounded-[3rem] p-10 shadow-2xl border border-slate-100 glow-hover">
    <img src="{{ asset('images/Academics/IMG_0400.jpg') }}" class="rounded-[2rem] object-cover w-full h-[300px] lab-image" alt="Materials of Construction Laboratory">
    <div>
        <div class="inline-block px-4 py-2 rounded-full bg-feu-green text-white text-sm font-bold mb-5">Room 101 • FIT Building</div>
        <h3 class="text-3xl font-black text-feu-green mb-5">Materials of Construction Laboratory</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Matcons laboratory is located at the ground floor (Room 101) of the FIT Building. It houses different equipment for testing materials used in construction such as concrete, steel, and asphalt. The centerpiece of the Matcons Lab is the Universal testing machine which is capable of checking compressive strength, shear strength and flexural strength of concrete, and tensile strength of steel.</p>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center bg-white rounded-[3rem] p-10 shadow-2xl border border-slate-100 glow-hover">
    <img src="{{ asset('images/Academics/IMG_0392.jpg') }}" class="rounded-[2rem] object-cover w-full h-[300px] lab-image" alt="Geotechnical Engineering Laboratory">
    <div>
        <div class="inline-block px-4 py-2 rounded-full bg-feu-green text-white text-sm font-bold mb-5">Room 1004 • FIT Building</div>
        <h3 class="text-3xl font-black text-feu-green mb-5">Geotechnical Engineering Laboratory</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Geotech Lab is located at the 10th floor (Room 1004) of FIT Building. It houses the equipment used for Geotechnical Engineering 1 (Soil Mechanics) and Geotechnical Engineering 2 (Foundation Engineering).</p>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center bg-white rounded-[3rem] p-10 shadow-2xl border border-slate-100 glow-hover">
    <img src="{{ asset('images/Academics/IMG_0410.jpg') }}" class="rounded-[2rem] object-cover w-full h-[300px] lab-image" alt="Hydraulics Laboratory">
    <div>
        <div class="inline-block px-4 py-2 rounded-full bg-feu-green text-white text-sm font-bold mb-5">Room 908 • FIT Building</div>
        <h3 class="text-3xl font-black text-feu-green mb-5">Hydraulics Laboratory</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Hydraulics Lab is located at the 9th floor (Room 908) of the FIT Building. It houses the equipment and apparatus needed for the fluid mechanics and hydraulics laboratory experiments.</p>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}

